# EVAL-CONFINEMENT-001 — Linux Landlock evaluator boundary

Date: 2026-09-29. Owner-selected OS filesystem isolation (see
`continuation-handoff.md` §Immediate blocker). Working tree: uncommitted on
`handover/h0-bundle-import` after `8143443`. **Development evidence only** —
exact-source/native CI has not run for this change, and no fuzz/replay ran.

## What landed

- `crates/gripsack-process/src/confinement.rs`: `Boundary` (read/read-write
  roots), `Ruleset::assemble` (Landlock ruleset built parent-side; the child
  applies only `PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS` + `LANDLOCK_RESTRICT_SELF` and, for `#!`
  runtimes, one `/proc/self/fd` rule — no allocation in `pre_exec`), and
  `runtime_read_roots` (program dir, `ldd` libraries, `#!` interpreter chain
  including `/usr/bin/env NAME` resolution, python prefix/stdlib via an
  argv[0]-faithful probe). `EXECUTE` is handled but granted only at `/`:
  running a binary never widens the read/write boundary; Deno's own permission
  model still denies evaluated-code process spawning.
- `OperatorEnvironment::with_evaluator_temp` redirects TMPDIR/TMP/TEMP to the
  private evaluator scratch; `PreparedEvaluation` provisions
  `$GRIPSACK_HOME/{deno-cache,eval-tmp}` and records runtime roots;
  `Frontend::run_bounded` assembles the per-launch boundary (captured roots,
  input directory, cache/scratch, runtime roots, runtime home, operator PATH
  dirs) and confines the invocation. Any assembly failure is an operational
  error before spawn — evaluation never runs unconfined.
- macOS: `Ruleset::assemble` returns `Unsupported`; the evaluator fails closed.
  That lane needs a qualified seatbelt design before native CI can pass.
- e2e harness: session-scoped `confined_runtime` fixture puts one deno copy on
  PATH (the operator executable space the boundary grants); wrapper-based
  fixtures exec it by PATH; the pause harness rendezvous moved under the
  evaluator's private scratch.
- Five ownership/lineage tests migrated to the approved-adoption resume flow
  (`test_destination_ownership.py`, `test_ownership_modes.py`) — they still
  asserted the removed single-shot auto-approve adopt behavior.

