## Honest limits

- macOS evaluation currently fails closed (`Unsupported`); the macOS CI lane
  cannot pass eval-dependent jobs until a seatbelt boundary lands and is
  natively qualified. This is the owner's fail-closed requirement, recorded as
  the open R1 leaf.
- `EXECUTE`-at-root means an operator-selected runtime may exec any binary;
  those binaries still inherit the read/write rules unchanged, and Deno denies
  spawning by evaluated code. Reading an executed binary is allowed anywhere
  only when its directory is an operator PATH entry, the runtime home, or an
  explicitly derived root — that is the operator's declared executable space.
- `ldd`/python-prefix probing trusts the operator-selected runtime (never repo
  bytes). A hostile operator runtime is outside this boundary by definition.
- Landlock itself, kernel correctness and host integrity are trusted, not
  proved. No Landlock kernel theorem or formal refinement is claimed.
- The earlier M-V6/M-V7 exact-candidate CI (36557008541) predates this change
  and does not qualify it. Exact-source CI for this tree has not been
  dispatched.
